+\subsection{Objects and theorem correspondence}
+The grouped model is \lean{MOR34.Model}, with the hypotheses of Section 2 in \lean{WellFormed}. Binary points are finite subsets of items, interpreted as indicator vectors. A paper item in position $r$ corresponds to Lean index $r-1$; the integer cut label itself is unchanged, and cut $r$ separates Lean indices below $r$ from those at least $r$. Counts use natural numbers with explicit upper bounds, equivalently the bounded nonnegative integer counts in~\eqref{eq:Z}. \lean{prefixSet}, \lean{Tight}, \lean{Exchange}, and \lean{componentCountMap} represent $p(z)$, $T$, feasible exchange edges, and $A$, respectively. The input candidate coefficient function is often named \lean{v} in the top-level Lean statements; it is the paper's $c$.
